  "armAUnderInvestigation": "Arm A scored 0 on every cell run so far while B and C passed, but the arm-A agent transcript shows it completing the task (dialogue-parser: 204 nodes, 321 edges, both output files reported written). A skill that is merely unhelpful does not produce a completed solve that grades zero. The leading hypothesis is a defect in arm A's own materialization or grading \u2014 it is the only arm whose graded workspace carries an extra .jinn-demo1-skills/ directory, and the only arm passed a --plugin-dir argument. Until that is diagnosed, NO arm comparison from these cells is meaningful in either direction.",
  "whyNotAResult": [
    "n=1 replicate on 3 tasks. The design calls for a rehearsal to size the run and a pre-registered official slate.",
    "Arm C passed on every task where it ran, which is the manipulation check failing: when the no-instruction control solves the task, the content has no detectable effect to deliver and A-versus-B is uninformative by the pre-declared rule.",
    "No power analysis, no MDE, no lock, no pre-registration anchor. Nothing here is a locked official run.",
    "The agent ran on the host rather than in the task image, which is a recorded deviation, not the sealed design."
  ]
